+# Broadcom compatibility research
+
+Accessed 2026-08-14.
+
+- [VMware Cloud Foundation - Upgrade Bundle Details](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/327207/vmware-cloud-foundation-upgrade-bundle.html) — supplied the published 4.5.1.0, 5.2.1.0, and 5.2.2.0 component builds and bundle identifiers used to compare the live BOM with the pinned snapshot.
+- [Upgrade VMware Cloud Foundation (VCF) 4.x and 5.x](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/405275/upgrade-vmware-cloud-foundation-vcf-4x-a.html) — confirmed the core sequence and the prerequisite roles: health/backups/bundles/prechecks, followed by SDDC Manager, NSX, vCenter, and ESXi; this workload-domain-only plan starts at NSX because the fleet management domain and SDDC Manager are already at target.
+- [Product Interoperability Matrix](https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Interoperability?col=285%2C&row=0%2C) — consulted for the vCenter, ESXi, and NSX target interoperability decision represented by the release gates.
+- [Broadcom Compatibility Guide](https://compatibilityguide.broadcom.com/search?program=software) — consulted for the ESXi 8.0 Update 3 hardware-compatibility gate that applies to all three workload hosts.
+- [Upgrade Sequence from VCF 4.5.1.0 to 5.2.1.0](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/418641/upgrade-sequence-from-vcf-4510-to-5210-r.html) — confirmed 5.2.1 as the supported first target from 4.5.1 and the NSX 4.2.1 evaluation/precheck dependency represented in the first hop.
